# The deployed asset set should be the page, not the project.
#
# This directory is deployed whole, so without this file the docs, the database schema and the
# tests are all fetchable on the hostname. Nothing in them is secret -- they are public in this
# repository -- but they are not the site, and every one of them is a file an attacker reads
# first to learn how the thing is wired.
#
# gitignore syntax. The platform already withholds `_headers`, `_redirects`, `_routes.json`,
# `_worker.js`, `functions/`, `node_modules/`, `.git/` and `.wrangler/` without being asked.
#
# ⚠ Read this before trusting the file. The classic Pages uploader walks the directory against
# a FIXED ignore list (the one above) and does not read this file -- only the newer static-asset
# uploader does. So until this project moves to that pipeline, this file states the intent and
# changes nothing, and `curl -I <host>/README.md` still answers 200. The fix that works on the
# deployment shape we have today is a `_routes.json` that sends these paths to the Function,
# which answers 404 to anything outside `/api/`.

README.md
CLAUDE.md
schema.sql
test/
